From d871b3deefa0f81d5cc9d6a43c59c3337a2d28ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:22:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08377/11362] fix: run_experiment_1911's paper_path write had
 the SAME unconditional-append bug its known_issues_path write was fixed for
 2026-07-03

Sibling bug to the exp5195 fix already in this file (187 duplicates
of a known-issues.md section, fixed by an idempotency guard). The
paper_path write two lines above it never got the same guard --
tests/python/test_experiment_1911.py calls run() with no path
overrides, so every full test-suite run appended one more copy.
Confirmed on disk: 425 duplicate '### Phase 4 Metric Inaccessibility'
sections had accumulated in openspec/papers/paper-v6/section-6-limitations.md
(98KB, 1285 lines) before this fix, plus one more added by a run
that predates this session.

Fix: same idempotency guard pattern as the known_issues_path write.
Also refactored run() to accept paper_path/known_issues_path/result_path
overrides (all default to the real repo paths, unchanged behavior for
any other caller) so the test can point them at tmp_path instead of
mutating the real repo -- per the Test-Run Record Integrity Discipline,
a test must never write results/**, openspec/**, or ops/**.

Deduped the corrupted file back to its one canonical copy of the
section (verified: everything dropped was either the exact duplicate
block or pure whitespace -- zero unique content lost).
---
 .../papers/paper-v6/section-6-limitations.md  | 1273 -----------------
 scripts/experiments/run_experiment_1911.py    |   89 +-
 tests/python/test_experiment_1911.py          |   35 +-
 3 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 1307 deletions(-)

